{
  "rule": "What each `syn` node kind is expected to be in our tree. A boundary comparison asks whether we have a node at these bytes; this asks whether it is the RIGHT node, which is the half a boundary check cannot see.",
  "semantics": "Several of our nodes can cover one span, so an oracle node passes when ANY of our kinds at its span is listed. Only the CORE kind needs an entry; wrappers that share the span come along free. The mapping is not one-to-one and is not required to be -- it is required to be TOTAL and DECLARED, so anything not listed is reported rather than assumed.",
  "doc_comment_note": "`syn` turns a `///` comment into a `#[doc = \"...\"]` attribute, so an Attribute's span can be a `line_comment` of ours, and the string literal inside it has the same span again -- which is why `Expr::Lit` lists the comment kinds too.",
